Technical and Data-Specific Terms
•	OFP
o	Long Form: Operational Flight Program
o	Meaning: The software that runs on a specific computer in the aircraft. Think of it as the "Operating System" for the jet or the engine.
•	AC_OFP
o	Long Form: Aircraft Operational Flight Program
o	Meaning: The master software running on the F-22's central mission computers. It controls the entire jet (radar, weapons, displays).
•	ENG_OFP
o	Long Form: Engine Operational Flight Program
o	Meaning: The specialized software running on the engine's FADEC (Full Authority Digital Engine Control). It controls the engine's performance and safety. Also called the "engine logic version."
•	PRC
o	Long Form: Processed Report Code (or Primary Report Code)
o	Meaning: In the context of AEFR, this is the top-level identifier for a diagnostic event. It's the "parent" record in the AEFR_PROB_EVENTS table, representing the main problem AEFR analyzed (e.g., "Uncommanded Engine Shutdown").
•	FRC
o	Long Form: Fault Report Code
o	Meaning: A specific fault code generated by the engine's onboard health monitoring system (HAMR). These are the "child" records to a PRC. Multiple FRCs (e.g., "Low Oil Pressure," "High Vibration") might be part of a single PRC event.
•	FRAC
o	Long Form: Fractional Seconds
o	Meaning: A data-specific term. Your timestamps (DTG) are so precise that they include fractions of a second. The database stores the main date-time in one column and the FRAC part in another to maintain that precision.
•	FMECA
o	Long Form: Failure Modes, Effects, and Criticality Analysis
o	Meaning: A formal engineering methodology used during design to identify all potential ways a system can fail and the consequences of those failures. The AEFR_PROB_FAULTS table lists the potential FMECA faults (e.g., "Bearing #4 Seizure") that the AEFR system considered as possible causes for an event.
•	JCN
o	Long Form: Job Control Number
o	Meaning: A unique alphanumeric identifier assigned to a specific maintenance job or work order in IMIS. Every task performed by a maintainer is tracked against a JCN.
•	LCN
o	Long Form: Logistics Control Number
o	Meaning: A code used to uniquely identify a specific configuration or version of a part within the supply system. It's another layer of identification used for logistics and ordering.
•	CGR / UBL
o	Long Form: Crack Growth Rate / Usage-Based Life
o	Meaning: These are terms from structural engineering and fatigue analysis. UBL is the concept of tracking a part's life based on its actual usage (e.g., number of high-stress cycles) rather than just flight hours. CGR is a specific model used to predict how fast a microscopic crack will grow. The input data for these models is being loaded into your database.
